      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Symptoms that persist after operations for angle-closure glaucoma arise from different causes. In the presence of open peripheral iridectomies miotics may be beneficial or may close angles; wide pupil dilatation by phenylephrine used to diminish posterior synechiae may close angles; cycloplegic mydriatics will close some angles and open others. Unexpected bizarre reactions to eye drops may occur. Persistent chronic glaucoma will be more common after laser iridotomy than after correctly assessed filtering operations. The importance of gonioscopy in diagnosis and management is emphasised."},
